The worlds of energy, transport and artificial intelligence are colliding and Ohme is at the heart of this new era. By using technology and data integrations to connect cars, chargers, people, energy providers and more, Ohme has a powerful platform that puts the consumer at the core.

Ohme has been selling its chargers to consumers since mid 2019 and has had exponential growth since. We are now operating in multiple countries and have partnerships with the likes of VW Group, Hyundai, Volvo, Octopus Energy, and other innovative brands.

We are scaling up the business and are building out the team for rapid growth. If you’re interested joining a fast-growing cleantech venture on a data and AI-first journey to speed up the global transition to clean, affordable energy, read on!
As a Senior Data Engineer, you will take technical ownership of designing, building, and scaling the data-driven services that power Ohme’s core business operations and smart energy platform. You will drive the engineering of high-impact data products, working at the intersection of data engineering, software architecture, and product innovation, you will ensure our data products are resilient, scalable, and delivered with low latency.&nbsp;

Key Responsibilities&nbsp;

- Collaborate: Work with data engineers, software engineers, the data innovation team, and other stakeholders to understand data requirements and deliver innovative solutions.&nbsp;

- Architect &amp; Build Data Products: Design, implement, and maintain scalable backend data services, ingestion engines, and APIs (REST / GraphQL / Event-driven) that expose data across internal systems and customer-facing features.&nbsp;

- Automate: Utilize Infrastructure as Code (IaC) tools, especially AWS Cloud Development Kit (CDK), to automate the deployment and management of data infrastructure.&nbsp;

- Product Mindset: Treat data as a product, caring about latency, API design, stability, user experience, and business impact.&nbsp;

- Optimize: Monitor and optimize the performance of data systems to ensure reliability and efficiency.&nbsp;

- Ensure Quality: Ensure data quality and integrity through rigorous testing and validation processes.&nbsp;

About You&nbsp;

- Proven professional experience as a data engineer building data platforms and APIs within AWS (S3, Lambda, Glue, Athena, Eventbridge, DynamoDB, API Gateway, Appsync) and Snowflake&nbsp;

- Possess strong IaC (preferably AWS CDK) and Python skills.&nbsp;

- Any experience with AWS Kinesis / Apache Flink or other real time streaming analytics setup is a bonus.&nbsp;

- Ideally, you come from a software engineering background and are familiar with common practices such as environment separation, CICD, TDD, and Agile methodologies.&nbsp;

- Comfortable working with Git and the command line.&nbsp;

- Excellent problem-solving and analytical skills, with a great engineering mindset.&nbsp;&nbsp;

- Knowledge of the electric vehicle industry is a plus.&nbsp;

Benefits

You’ll get to work in a fast-paced and rapidly growing scale-up with global ambitions that is cutting edge, passionate about sustainability and seeks to make the world a better place.

Our benefits:

- Competitive salary and bonus

- London Office - 3 days a week in the office

- Private Health Insurance

- Pension Scheme

- Life Assurance Scheme with death in service benefit of 4x salary

- Income Protection Scheme for long term illness

- Ride to Work Scheme

- Payroll Giving Scheme

- Season Ticket Loan to spread cost of travel over 12 months

- Eye Test every 2 years

Ohme is an equal opportunity employer. Diversity, Equity and Inclusion are at the heart of what we do and we encourage a culture where everyone can be themselves at work. We actively seek out a diverse range of talent and our policies ensure that every job application and employee is treated fairly, with equal opportunity to succeed and to feel included.

THE ROLE 📝&nbsp;

We’re looking for a Reporting &amp; Data Analyst to help Form3 develop a more reliable, scalable and accessible reporting capability across the organisation.&nbsp;

This is a six-month fixed-term contract with two clear priorities: completing and enhancing the Customer Service reporting suite in AWS QuickSight, and building trusted, reusable datasets that enable teams to create and maintain their own reporting.&nbsp;

You’ll work across the business to improve data quality, reduce manual reporting and establish stronger documentation, governance and knowledge transfer for the future.&nbsp;

- Complete and enhance the Customer Service reporting suite and reporting deck in AWS QuickSight.&nbsp;

- Design, build and document reusable datasets for multiple reporting use cases.&nbsp;

- Integrate key business systems into curated reporting datasets.&nbsp;

- Translate stakeholder questions into clear data and dashboard requirements.&nbsp;

- Establish consistent business metrics, definitions and reporting logic.&nbsp;

- Automate manual reporting and duplicated data preparation where possible.&nbsp;

- Validate reporting outputs and investigate data-quality issues.&nbsp;

- Provide knowledge transfer to internal teams and support a longer-term reporting roadmap.&nbsp;

&nbsp;

WE’RE LOOKING FOR 🔍&nbsp;

Essential&nbsp;

- Experience in a Reporting Analyst, Data Analyst, BI Analyst or similar role.&nbsp;

- Hands-on experience building and maintaining dashboards using AWS QuickSight or a comparable BI platform.&nbsp;

- Practical experience using SQL and Python for reporting, data transformation or analysis.&nbsp;

- Experience working with multiple data sources and translating stakeholder requirements into accurate, maintainable reporting.&nbsp;

- A self-sufficient and pragmatic approach, with the ability to take ownership and deliver within a focused six-month engagement.&nbsp;

&nbsp;

Desirable&nbsp;

- Experience using Amazon Athena or a similar cloud-based data querying service.&nbsp;

- Experience creating curated datasets for self-service reporting.&nbsp;

- Experience improving data quality, reporting governance and technical documentation.&nbsp;

- Experience working in a start-up, scale-up or small team where you have had broad ownership.&nbsp;

&nbsp;

TECH STACK ⚙️&nbsp;

- AWS QuickSight - building dashboards, reporting suites and reusable datasets.&nbsp;

- SQL - querying, transforming and validating reporting data.&nbsp;

- Python - supporting data transformation, automation and reporting workflows.&nbsp;

- Business and operational systems - integrating data sources into trusted reporting datasets.

&nbsp;

INTERVIEW PROCESS ✍️&nbsp;

Stage 1: Screening Call with Talent Team&nbsp;

Stage 2: Practical Technical Task&nbsp;

Stage 3: Interview with the Hiring Manager, including a discussion of your technical task and your approach to reporting, data quality, stakeholder requirements and self-service analytics&nbsp;

We always aim to stick to the above process, however there may be occasions when an additional interview stage is needed for us to be sure we’re hiring the right fit for the role.&nbsp;

&nbsp;

HIRING LOCATIONS📍&nbsp;

Here are the locations that we are hiring from for this position.&nbsp;

- United Kingdom&nbsp;

All new joiners start their first day in our office to collect the equipment needed to work remotely. We'll also arrange for some of your team to come in to say hi, ensuring you're supported and have a positive first few days with Form3!&nbsp;&nbsp;

&nbsp;

BENEFITS 🏝️&nbsp;

Form3 are a 100% remote, flexible business and are able to offer part-time working arrangements. We believe this enables our people to achieve amazing things with a healthy work-life balance.&nbsp;

For further information on what it’s like to work here, and for more information on our full benefits package, visit our careers page. If you have any other questions, we’d be happy to discuss these with your during the interview process.&nbsp;

&nbsp;&nbsp;

ABOUT FORM3 💭&nbsp;

Revolutionising the world of payments with our cloud-native, multi-cloud platform. For more information about Form3, check out the following pages:&nbsp;

What we do | Life at Form3 | Benefits | Payments Cannot Fail Series | .Tech Podcast&nbsp;
&nbsp;

OUR DEI&amp;B COMMITMENT&nbsp;

We hire talented people from a variety of backgrounds and experiences and are committed to a work environment based on diversity, open-mindedness and curiosity. We’re united by our company values (we even created them together!) and we celebrate our unique differences.&nbsp;

Our employee lifecycle processes are designed to embrace equal opportunity and prevent discrimination against our people regardless of personal characteristics. It is our strong belief that the more inclusive and belonging we are as a business, the better our work will be.&nbsp;

As an inclusive employer, we guarantee to interview all neurodiverse and physically disabled applicants who meet the minimum criteria for this role. We also encourage candidates to notify us of any reasonable adjustments that may be required during the recruitment process. This includes providing job adverts in alternative, accessible formats or adjustments required at interview stage.&nbsp;

If you consider yourself to be neurodiverse or physically disabled under the UN definition of disability and would like to be considered under this scheme and/or require any reasonable adjustments please let us know by sending an email to careers@form3.tech clearly stating your consent for us to process this data. 

For more information please refer to our Recruitment Data Policy.&nbsp;
